msgid "is also accepted for existing Stripe configurations. Handlers retrieve current Stripe resources rather than trusting an older event's snapshot. Local webhook writes use serializable transactions, so failed processing rolls back and Stripe can retry. Checkout, subscription and invoice IDs identify existing records; replaying a checkout neither consumes a new cart nor extends a fixed-duration entitlement."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/generated-docs-from-md-files/@taon-dev/e-commerce/README.component.html:32
msgid "Expired checkouts cancel pending orders and release stock/purchase reservations. Cart items remain available for another checkout. Leaving Stripe through"
msgstr ""

